[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407315019","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119338#issuecomment-4407315019","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119338","id":4407315019,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBrJKSw","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T14:41:49Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T14:41:49Z","body":"I almost forgot to ask, would it be considered a breaking change even if there hasn't been a stable release with the previous `search_bar_enabled_on_item_count` property? If so, do we need to add some kind of migration code for it?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407315019/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407429623","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119338#issuecomment-4407429623","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119338","id":4407429623,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBrQJ9w","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T14:59:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T14:59:17Z","body":"> I also threw in `ADD_GROUP(\"Search Bar\", \"search_bar_\")`, since there's a handful of search properties already, and it's possible we'll be adding even more in the future, if/when `FuzzySearch` is exposed.\r\n\r\nThinking about this some more, I guess it does look a bit weird to have both the groups and the dynamic hiding of the fuzzy search properties.\r\n\r\nDo I revert the groups, or do I remove the dynamic hiding, or do we go with both?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4407429623/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409485695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119338#issuecomment-4409485695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119338","id":4409485695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBtNpfw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T20:07:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T20:26:36Z","body":"> I almost forgot to ask, would it be considered a breaking change even if there hasn't been a stable release with the previous search_bar_enabled_on_item_count property?\r\n\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n> Thinking about this some more, I guess it does look a bit weird to have both the groups and the dynamic hiding of the fuzzy search properties. Do I revert the groups, or do I remove the dynamic hiding, or do we go with both?\r\n\r\nUse `PROPERTY_HINT_GROUP_ENABLE`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409485695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409882967","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119338#issuecomment-4409882967","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119338","id":4409882967,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBtl5Vw","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T21:10:42Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T21:10:42Z","body":"You somewhat misunderstood my request. I don't think we should do away with the trigger on item count, but instead we should add a toggle on top of it, where then all related properties will depend upon, and make the item trigger's minimal value 1.\r\n\r\nAlso, the toggle should be in the section, for example:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"246\" height=\"36\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be885589-7d64-47b5-a69e-f399020020a8\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409882967/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4411020312","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119338#issuecomment-4411020312","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119338","id":4411020312,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBurUGA","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-09T01:50:15Z","updated_at":"2026-05-09T01:50:15Z","body":"> I don't think we should do away with the trigger on item count, but instead we should add a toggle on top of it\r\n\r\nThat was indeed a misunderstanding on my part, my bad.\r\n\r\nI've pushed something that hopefully lines up better with what you had in mind, where it's a separate `search_bar_enabled` and `search_bar_min_item_count`.\r\n\r\nI do still think the minimum count thing is a bit odd-looking, but I guess it's less so with the separate toggle.\r\n\r\nA couple of notes about this latest iteration:\r\n\r\n1. `search_bar_enabled` now represents the overall enabled state, and not the actual visibility of it, unlike before. So anyone wanting the visibility state would have to derive it from `search_bar_enabled` and `search_bar_min_item_count`.\r\n2. Instead of lazily setting search bar visibility in `PopupMenu::set_visible`, I've moved it to be done in `PopupMenu::_menu_changed` instead, as well as the relevant setters, which means search bar visibility should react to state changes appropriately, fixing the above mentioned bug.\r\n3. The default/minimum value of `search_bar_min_item_count` is 0, not 1, since I figured the search bar should be visible by default even if you `clear()` the `PopupMenu`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4411020312/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4425602920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119338#issuecomment-4425602920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119338","id":4425602920,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABB8lXaA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-11T22:15:07Z","updated_at":"2026-05-11T22:15:07Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4425602920/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]